  "steps": [
    "Pat the chicken thighs dry and season with a little of the salt and black pepper.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a wide pan over medium-high heat. Brown the chicken on both sides for 3 to 4 minutes per side, then transfer to a plate.",
    "Lower the heat to medium and add the onion. Cook for 5 to 6 minutes until softened and lightly golden, then stir in the garlic, cumin, paprika, ground coriander, turmeric and cinnamon for 30 seconds.",
    "Add the canned tomatoes, water, remaining salt and the browned chicken. Stir well, bring to a gentle simmer, cover and cook for 30 minutes.",
    "Stir in the olives, lemon wedges and lemon juice. Simmer uncovered for 10 to 15 minutes until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Finish with the chopped parsley and serve hot.",
    "If you like, serve with rice or gluten-free bread to soak up the sauce."
